    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I've read some source files but the SKILL.md file was truncated. I can see the protocol has version 0.4.0, canonical URL https://clawhub.ai/xiwan/agent-linguo, signature format, security levels P/B/E, and the three markers. I need to read the full SKILL.md file to get all protocol details.",
  "plan": "Read the complete SKILL.md file using head with more lines or less, and check the references directory for additional protocol details.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -500 skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md file is still being truncated. I need to read the complete file to get all protocol details including handshake rules, security levels, and field mappings.",
  "plan": "Use tail or read the file in chunks to get the complete content. Also check the references directory for additional files.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "wc -l skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | head -300\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | tail -400\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md file has 301 lines but output is being truncated. I need to read it in smaller chunks to capture all the protocol details.",
  "plan": "Read the file in smaller segments using sed to get lines 1-150, 151-301 to capture all content.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,150p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '151,301p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The output is still being truncated. I need to save the file content to a temporary file or use a different approach to capture all the data.",
  "plan": "Copy the SKILL.md file to work/ directory and read it there, or use python to read and display the full content.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cp skill_context/SKILL.md work/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"with open('work/SKILL.md', 'r') as f: print(f.read())\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The output is still being truncated by the terminal. I need to save the content to a file and then process it.",
  "plan": "Use python to write the file content to a new file, then use cat to display it.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"with open('skill_context/SKILL.md', 'r') as f: content = f.read(); open('work/full_skill.md', 'w').write(content)\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat work/full_skill.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The terminal is truncating long outputs. I need to use a different approach - I'll read the file using python and save it to disk, then verify the content was captured correctly.",
  "plan": "Use python to read the SKILL.md file and save it to work/, then check the file size and use grep to extract specific sections of interest.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 << 'EOF'\nwith open('skill_context/SKILL.md', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\nwith open('work/skill_full.txt', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(content)\nprint(f\"Saved {len(content)} characters\")\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "wc -c work/skill_full.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"Security\" work/skill_full.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"handshake\" work/skill_full.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"handshake\\|Handshake\" work/skill_full.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I found the full SKILL.md content (7640 chars) and identified key sections. There's a reference file at skill_context/references/handshake.md that contains handshake details. I need to read that file and extract more protocol details.",
  "plan": "Read the handshake reference file and extract more details from the skill file using grep to get security levels, field mappings, and other protocol details.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/handshake.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -A 10 \"Security Level\" work/skill_full.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -B 2 -A 5 \"Field Mapping\" work/skill_full.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I found the handshake.md file with protocol details. The output is being truncated. I need to save all reference files and read them completely to extract all protocol information.",
  "plan": "Copy all reference files to work/ directory and use python to read them completely, then extract the key information needed for the reference document.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cp skill_context/references/* work/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 << 'EOF'\nwith open('work/handshake.md', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\nprint(content)\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

